{#- Front door banner artwork, shared by both masthead variants.

    Two pages render this: front-door-banner.njk (full-bleed teal band) and
    front-door-banner-inset.njk (inset panel, printable on a desktop printer).
    They differ ONLY in how the masthead meets the paper edge, so the markup
    lives here rather than in two files that would quietly drift apart while
    the client is choosing between them. Once one is picked, delete the other
    page and this can be folded back inline.

    The variant page sets `bannerVariant` in its front matter; Nunjucks
    includes inherit the template context, so it is readable here. -#}
<div class="canvas banner {{ bannerVariant }}">

    {# The wordmark is Book Jacket converted to outlines — NOT a webfont. The
       file was licensed for print through the sign shop; an @font-face rule
       would hand the binary to every visitor. Outlines ship no font file.

       inlineSvg rather than <img>: the artwork carries no fill of its own, so
       inside an <img> it renders black and CSS cannot reach in to recolour it.
       Inlined, .wordmark--light in piece.css gives it the cream letterform,
       teal outline and red offset — the same treatment as the site hero and
       the social pieces. #}
    <header class="banner-top">
        <div class="wordmark wordmark--light banner-wordmark">
            {% inlineSvg "/assets/thecafe.svg", "", site.name %}
        </div>
        {# Cream, not red. The masthead behind this is --teal, and red on teal
           is 1.3:1 — the one pairing the palette forbids outright. #}
        <p class="p-eyebrow banner-entrance ink-cream">Entrance</p>
        <div class="banner-filigree ink-cream">
            {% include "partials/filigree.njk" %}
        </div>
    </header>

    {# Two lines, not one. "Monday, October 5th" set large enough to read from
       the sidewalk does not fit across an 11in sheet, and shrinking it to fit
       would make the date no bigger than the hours below it. Splitting lets
       the date itself stay the largest thing on the banner. #}
    <section class="banner-announce">
        <p class="p-display-italic announce-kicker ink-teal">Restaurant opening</p>
        <p class="p-display announce-day ink-teal">{{ site.opening.dayName }}</p>
        <p class="p-display announce-date ink-accent">{{ site.opening.monthDay }}<sup>{{ site.opening.ordinal }}</sup></p>
    </section>

    <section class="banner-hours">
        <p class="p-label hours-label ink-accent">{{ site.opening.hoursLabel }}</p>
        <p class="p-display hours-days ink-teal">{{ site.opening.hoursDays }}</p>
        <p class="p-display hours-time ink-teal">{{ site.opening.opens.time }} <span class="ampm">{{ site.opening.opens.meridiem }}</span> &ndash; {{ site.opening.closes.time }} <span class="ampm">{{ site.opening.closes.meridiem }}</span></p>
    </section>

    <footer class="banner-footer">
        <div class="follow">
            {# Encodes https://www.facebook.com/LVCafeToGo at error-correction
               level H, so the code still scans with a corner scuffed or a
               thumbtack through it. Regenerate per studio/README.md. #}
            <div class="qr follow-qr">
                {% inlineSvg "/assets/qr-facebook.svg" %}
            </div>
            {# The handle breaks after the slash rather than running on one
               line. The banner faces out through the door glass, so the code
               is sized for a phone that has to focus through a reflective
               pane; a narrower caption is what buys that width back. #}
            <div class="follow-text">
                <p class="p-label follow-label ink-accent">Follow us</p>
                <p class="p-body follow-handle ink-teal">facebook.com/<br><strong>LVCafeToGo</strong></p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="contact">
            <p class="p-display contact-phone ink-teal">{{ site.phone }}</p>
            <p class="p-body contact-line">{{ site.email }}</p>
            <p class="p-body contact-line">{{ site.address.street }}</p>
            <p class="p-body contact-line">{{ site.address.locality }}, {{ site.address.region }} {{ site.address.postalCode }}</p>
        </div>
    </footer>

</div>
